<title>NORWAY: Norske Shell plugs North Sea exploration well.</title>
<headline>Norske Shell plugs North Sea exploration well.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norske Shell, as operator for licence 035 in block 30/11, has plugged and abandoned exploration well 30/11-5 in the North Sea without running a production test, the Oil Directorate said on Friday.</p>
<p>The well, drilled to a depth of 3,702 metres below sea level, was sited between the Frigg gas field and the Oseberg oil development. It showed only traces of hydrocarbons, the directorate said.</p>
<p>Norske Shell holds 100 percent of licence 035.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
